work um model  bitcoin protocol model identities are  the separate part and the transactions  basically go through the public in the  form of the ledger  so back to the paper as an additional  firewall a new key pair  should be used for each transaction to  keep them from being linked to a common  owner  some linking is still unavoidable with  multi-input transactions so kind of what  we were just discussing a moment ago  which necessary which necessarily reveal  that their inputs were owned by the same  owner  the risk is that if the owner of a key  is revealed  linking could reveal other transactions  that belonged to the same owner  now here's the important part where the  user gets the right to choose their  anonymity level in the case of a charity  for example they would likely if they're  legit  opt to possibly use the same public key  for all donations and expenditures  anyways this is so people could actually  see where the donation money was going  this is a business  or an organization that should be very  transparent  and this is a very easy way for people  to do that a corporation  with a lot of competition let's say  instead would probably choose to go the  secret route an anonymous route changing  their public key very often  so that it would be harder to track  where money is being spent  now obviously they would still be  required to report earnings um  you know the government for taxation  purposes and all of that so  that doesn't go away now this  optionality for anonymity is where the  debate is though i think it yields  the best of both worlds businesses and  organizations that should be transparent  now have an extremely simplistic way of  doing it business people in businesses  that have  a level of security invested in being  private  also have a simple way of doing so also  these options can even be married for a  perfect balance that  you can choose or your business can  choose so you can have your public funds  in one location the stuff you